# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kyacode — Go single-binary CLI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Compiled binaries / build output (regenerate with `go build ./cmd/kyacode`)
/bin/
/dist/
/kyacode
/kyacode.exe
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Go workspace / tool cache
go.work
go.work.sum

# Test & coverage output
*.test
coverage.out
*.cover

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# research/ is vendored third-party source + release artifacts (~1.4 GB)
# Only the analysis notes are kept in the repo; the downloaded ollama tree,
# its binaries and packed archives are ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/research/ollama/bin/
/research/ollama/*.tar.zst
/research/ollama/*.tar
/research/ollama/*.tgz
/research/ollama/release.json
# vendored upstream sources under research/ are reference-only, not our code
/research/ollama/src/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling / editor / OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.AppleDouble
# Windows OS droppings (this is a Windows dev box)
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor state: nothing here is tracked by decision
/.vscode/
/.idea/

# Qwen Code session scratch (wakeup/task state, not project source)
/.qwen/tmp/

# Node tooling under .opencode (deps + generated lockfiles are ignored by
# .opencode/.gitignore; keep the skills/ and commands/ sources tracked)
/.opencode/node_modules/
/.opencode/package.json
/.opencode/package-lock.json
/.opencode/bun.lock

# Stray shell-redirect accidents (e.g. an accidental `2>1` creates a file "1")
/1
/2
nohup.out
# local release-asset builds (kyacode-<os>-<arch>; real assets ship from CI)
/kyacode-*
# scratch generator scripts (one-off report builders)
/_gen.py

# Logs & temp
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — NEVER commit keys/tokens/credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# env files holding API keys / tokens (local overrides included)
.env
.env.*
.envrc
!.env.example
# key material of any shape
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Token-named artifacts are scoped to the repo ROOT on purpose: unscoped
# `*token*` silently dropped every future tokenstore.go / token_test.go /
# token_sweep fixture from a commit (the workspace-hygiene audit). The
# root rule keeps the old CONTAINS semantics (`/*token*` also covers
# gw_token.txt / oauth_keys.txt — a leading * in glob can be empty), while
# subdirectory token-named code/fixtures track normally and token-NAMED
# PROSE keeps the .md exception.
/*token*
!*token*.md
# credential stores, likewise root-scoped so an auth.json FIXTURE or a
# credentials.json schema file under internal/ never goes dark in a review
/credentials.json
/client_secret*.json
/auth.json
/.oauth_tokens.json
# preserved after chmod'd token files (paranoia: any .kyacode workdir copy)
.kyacode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent experiment scratch at the repo root — an untracked base64 blob or
# debug dump was one `git add .` away from a commit in a repo whose daily
# bread is a token tool (the workspace-hygiene audit's stray files: two
# *.b64 blobs, a -out.txt pair). Scope keeps fixtures and docs untouched.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.b64
/*-out.txt
/scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local agent tooling — per-machine scratch, never upload
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.agents/
/.claude/
/.qwen/
/.scratch/
/.out-of-scope/
/skills-lock.json
/.opencode/
